"3.1. Solving Linear Systems by Graphing www.ck12.org 3. Classify the following systems as consistent, inconsistent, independent or dependent. You may do this with or without graphing them. You do not need to ﬁnd the unique solution if there is one. 4. 4x−y = 8 y = 4x+3 5. 5x+y = 10 y = 5x+10 6. 2x−2y = 11 y = x+13 7. −7x+3y = −21 14x−6y = 42 8. y = −3 5x+1 3x+5y = 5 9. 6x−y = 18 y = 1 6x+3"
